ee":{"login":"akanil18","id":180043112,"node_id":"U_kgDOCrs9aA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180043112?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akanil18","html_url":"https://github.com/akanil18","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akanil18/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akanil18/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akanil18/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akanil18/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akanil18/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akanil18/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akanil18/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akanil18/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akanil18/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"author_association":"COLLABORATOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### What is the conjecture\nLet $K \\subset \\mathbb{R}^2$ be a planar convex body with a center of symmetry and containing the origin, and let $p > 1$ with conjugate exponent $q$ ($1/p + 1/q = 1$). The planar $L_p$-Rogers–Shephard inequality states that\n\n$$\n|K \\oplus_p -K| \\le \\Big( \\frac{2 \\Gamma(1 + 1/q)^2}{\\Gamma(1 + 2/q)} + 2 \\Big) |K|.\n$$\n\nEquality is known to hold whenever $K$ is a parallelogram with a vertex at the origin.\n\n**Conjecture (Fradelizi–Manui–Meyer–Ndiaye, 2026):** Among all planar convex bodies $K \\subset \\mathbb{R}^2$ having a center of symmetry and containing the origin, for any $p > 1$, equality in the above inequality holds only for parallelograms with a vertex at the origin.\n\n* **Source Paper:** *L_p-Rogers--Shephard type inequalities for L_p-zonoids and symmetric bodies* ([arXiv:2607.03582](https://arxiv.org/abs/2607.03582), [HTML](https://arxiv.org/html/2607.03582), [PDF](https://arxiv.org/pdf/2607.03582))\n* **Authors:** Matthieu Fradelizi, Auttawich Manui, Mark Meyer, Cheikh Saliou Ndiaye\n* **In-Paper Location:** [Conjecture 5 (Page 39)](https://arxiv.org/pdf/2607.03582#page=39) in Section \"Symmetric bodies\"\n* **OpenConjecture ID:** 4626 ([OpenConjecture](https://github.com/davisrbr/conjectures-arxiv))\n\n### Prerequisites needed\nAll required core theories are available in Mathlib4:\n* Convex sets and convex bodies: [`Mathlib.Analysis.Convex.Basic`](https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/Mathlib/Analysis/Convex/Basic.html)\n* Real Gamma function: [`Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Gamma.Basic`](https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/Mathlib/Analysis/SpecialFunctions/Gamma/Basic.html)\n* Lebesgue volume and measure in $\\mathbb{R}^2$: [`Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Measure.Lebesgue.Basic`](https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/Mathlib/MeasureTheory/Measure/Lebesgue/Basic.html)\n* Euclidean spaces and inner products: [`Mathlib.Analysis.InnerProductSpace.Basic`](https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/Mathlib/Analysis/InnerProductSpace/Basic.html)\n\n### Choose either option\n- [ ] I plan on adding this conjecture to the repository\n- [x] This issue is up for grabs: I would like to see this conjecture added by somebody else\n\nThis issue was generated by an AI agent and reviewed by me.","closed_by":{"login":"mo271","id":3491627,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM0OTE2Mjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3491627?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mo271","html_url":"https://github.com/mo271","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mo271/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mo271/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mo271/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://a